id: petrification
name: Petrification
uaType: magical
prerequisite: Magic Score of 8+
tpCost: 20
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCostPerTier: 10
requiresTarget: true
# "Target an Opponent who is not at Long Range" - refused before it is paid. "Make a Clash (Strike vs Strike/Dodge)";
# won, Guard Down to the end of the current turn, and a button for the second Clash, "you may" - (Cognitive vs
# Cognitive/Corporeal/Impulsive); won, a stack of Slowed to the end of the Combat Encounter, shed from the target's own
# card by destroying a wielded Weapon or a worn piece of Apparel, and gone if its user is Defeated (chat.mjs
# postPetrification).
petrifies: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  A Strike Clash at an Opponent not at Long Range: won, Guard Down this turn, and you may Clash (Cognitive vs
  Cognitive/Corporeal/Impulsive) - won, a stack of Slowed for the Encounter, shed by losing a Weapon or a piece of
  Apparel to dust; gone if you are Defeated.
text: >
  Petrification: You possess the capability of turning your opponents into inanimate objects, preventing them from
  fighting.
  –Ability Type: Magical
  –Prerequisites: Magic Score of 8+
  –TP Cost: 20
  –KP Cost: 10(T)
  –Maneuver Type: Standard
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –Minions: Non-Minion
  –Passive Bonus: N/A
  –Effect: Target an Opponent who is not at Long Range. Make a Clash (Strike vs Strike/Dodge) against that Opponent. If
  you win, they gain the Guard Down Combat Condition until the end of the current turn. Then, you may make a Clash
  (Cognitive vs Cognitive/Corporeal/Impulsive) against them. If you win this second Clash, they gain a stack of the
  Slowed Combat Condition until the end of the Combat Encounter. They can remove a stack of this Combat Condition by
  dropping a carried Weapon or removing a layer of Apparel. Whatever is dropped crumbles to dust and is destroyed.

  If the user of this Unique Ability is Defeated, all Characters suffering from the Slowed Combat Condition due to this
  character’s uses of Petrification stop suffering from those stack(s) of this Combat Condition.
